{{Quote|There is little middle ground in cutting down a tree and not cutting down a tree.|[[Qui-Gon Jinn]]|<ref name="QGJ 1">[[Age of Republic - Qui-Gon Jinn 1|''Age of Republic - Qui-Gon Jinn'' 1]]</ref>}}
'''Trees''' were a type of [[plant]] found on many [[planet]]s and [[moon]]s throughout [[the galaxy]]. They could stabilize soil, prevent erosion, filter pollution, and produce breathable air.<ref name="VE" /> Trees could not be seeded without ground.<ref name="The High Republic Adventures: Quest of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic Adventures: Quest of the Jedi]]''</ref> Some [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] such as the [[Wookiee]]s of the planet [[Kashyyyk]]<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> and the [[Ewok]]s of the [[Forest]] Moon of [[Endor]] made their homes in and around trees.<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> The [[Aleen Underworld|subterranean caverns]] of [[Aleen]] housed a species of tree-like sentients, the [[Kindalo]].<ref name="DB Kindalo">{{Databank|kindalo|Kindalo}}</ref> [[Bird]]s usually built nests in trees, though some species were known to make their homes in burrows beneath the ground.<ref name="Creature Safari">{{YJA|Creature Safari}}</ref> The fine wood particles created when a tree was cut, were known as sawdust.<ref name="Forest Defenders">{{YJA|Forest Defenders}}</ref>

On [[Ahch-To]], the [[Homeworld|birthplace]] of the [[Jedi Order]] and the location of the [[first Jedi Temple]], a [[Tree library|library]] existed inside of a [[uneti tree]], containing [[Jedi]] knowledge.<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>

On the planet [[Gloam]], there were trees that could uproot and move themselves to follow the tides of the seasonal lakes.<ref name="QFTHC">''[[The High Republic: Quest for the Hidden City]]''</ref>

Despite featuring a largely desolate [[desert]] landscape,<ref name="CL2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> the planet [[Tatooine]] featured trees around the [[time]] of the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="GA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> However, trees were unimaginable to [[Luke Skywalker]] during his time on Tatooine, as the [[human]] had never seen them in the landscape of the world.<ref name="ANH Illustrated">''[[A New Hope: The Princess, the Scoundrel, and the Farm Boy]]''</ref>

[[Wroshyr tree]]s were of great importance in Wookiee culture. A saying in their native [[language]] of [[Shyriiwook]] was that "''The trees are life''," though this was only a rough translation.<ref name="Mighty Chewbacca">''[[The Mighty Chewbacca in the Forest of Fear!]]''</ref>

It was possible for trees to be steeped in the [[dark side of the Force]]. [[Jedi Master]] [[Cohmac Vitus]] had encountered trees deep in the dark side at some point before [[232 BBY]].<ref name="ITD">''[[The High Republic: Into the Dark]]''</ref>

One faction on the [[planet]] [[Bri'n]] revered and protected their trees. That faction had a [[Priestess of Wood]] to protect them. On the other end of the dispute was the [[Metal Clan]], which hated and sought to destroy the trees.<ref name="QGJ 1" />

The [[Tree of Te Ani'la|trees of Te Ani'la]] were used as ornamental plants for the [[Imperial Academy of Mandalore|Royal Academy of Government]] on [[Mandalore]].<ref name="VE" />

